---
title: Smoked Rosemary Boulevardier Sour
servings: 2
prep-time: 10 minutes
cook-time: 0 minutes
tags: [mixology, cocktails, holiday-cocktails, boulevardier, smoked-cocktail]
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DSp-bkRD69a/
image: https://scontent-iad3-1.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.71878-15/587776433_1402281444600792_7884693029588920670_n.jpg?stp=cmp1_dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=101&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=ES0nGB_ttpcQ7kNvwGT4DNw&_nc_oc=AdlNCfo48_0fQB8YCFxmCwJZCANPY92QeLYdyphGZLL_9v7l_a4z3JNiFdu58-a5tGA&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-1.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=K_n0c9JS_aijyBhOoOpVng&oh=00_AfmYmMpCSJjuGLdU_vIBNCz1J-YxTEKGGWtiWF2xhxItuQ&oe=6955F335
---

Chill two #rocks glasses{} and begin by smoking @rosemary{2%sprig} over them to perfume the rims and the air around the drinks, ~{15%seconds}.

In a #cocktail shaker{}, add @bourbon{3%oz}, @campari{2%oz}, @sweet vermouth{2%oz}, @lemon juice{1.5%oz}, @simple syrup{1%oz}, and @cinnamon{0.25%tsp}. Fill with ice and shake ~{15%seconds} until well chilled. Strain into two #rocks glasses{} filled with fresh ice.

Finish by garnishing each drink with a rosemary sprig to reinforce the aroma; place @rosemary{1%sprig} in each glass.